  "post": {
    "youtube_title": "Jewelry rendering: why diamonds need dark facets",
    "caption": "Gem labs judge a diamond's look by brightness, fire and scintillation, and GIA and AGS both count the contrast between its light and dark areas. In a jewelry render the stone needs bright highlights and darker areas around it, or it turns white and plain. The renders in this video were made with HeyGema.",
